-- title:
--   Integral closedness of the chart ring at the j-pole
-- statement:
--   Fix a natural number $N$, nonzero, and a prime $\ell$. Write $\mathbb{Z}\ell$ for the coefficient ring [`GaloisRep.ratLocalizedAt ℓ`](def/GaloisRep_Flat.html#L8) and $F$ for the field `modularFunctionFieldFull N`, on which $\mathbb{Z}\ell$ acts as a subring; let `jFull N` be the element `jq` of $F$ (the modular function $j$, together with its membership in the full modular function field of level $N$). The subalgebra `chartAlgInf N ℓ` of $F$ over $\mathbb{Z}\ell$ is `chartAlg N ℓ` applied to the singleton $\{(\mathrm{jFull}\,N)^{-1}\}$, i.e. the set of all $x \in F$ that are integral over the $\mathbb{Z}\ell$-subalgebra generated by $j^{-1}$ (the stated closure properties under sums, products and the structure map make this a subalgebra). The theorem asserts that this subalgebra, viewed as a ring in its own right, is integrally closed: every element of its fraction field that is integral over it already lies in it.
--
--   This is the standard fact that an integral closure inside a field is integrally closed, applied to the ring of the chart around the cusp $j = \infty$ used in the construction of the Igusa scheme [`ModularCurve.IgusaScheme`](def/ModularCurve_IgusaScheme.html#L255), the pushout of the two chart spectra along their common middle piece. It feeds the reducedness and integral-closedness statements for the base change of this chart ring, such as [`ModularCurve.IgusaScheme.isIntegrallyClosed_tensor_chartAlgInf_of_charZero`](thm.html#ModularCurve.IgusaScheme.isIntegrallyClosed_tensor_chartAlgInf_of_charZero) and [`ModularCurve.IgusaScheme.isReduced_chartAlgInf_tensor`](thm.html#ModularCurve.IgusaScheme.isReduced_chartAlgInf_tensor).
